# Known gitleaks false positives, one fingerprint per line.
#
# A fingerprint is commit:path:rule:line, so an entry here can only ever
# silence that exact finding in that exact commit. It cannot mask a real
# secret added later, in another file, or by another rule. Add an entry only
# for a value that is demonstrably not a credential, with a note saying why.
#
# On pull_request events the gitleaks action scans the branch's whole commit
# range rather than the working tree, so a placeholder removed in a later
# commit still has to be acknowledged here.

# A placeholder bearer token in the cURL to Fetch Converter's "Load example"
# sample string, matched by the curl-auth-header rule. It was never a real
# credential: it read "sk-example-token" and pointed at api.example.com, the
# RFC 2606 reserved documentation domain. The sample was rewritten in
# 351165c to carry no Authorization header at all, so the current tree is
# clean and this entry covers only the superseded commit.
